# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows (`core.autocrlf=true` by default) hands the
# Windows CI runner CRLF working copies, and `prettier --check` - which formats
# to LF - then fails on every file while the Linux runners pass. Pinning the
# line ending here makes the checkout identical on all three platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and pre-rendered assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.har binary

# Generated lockfile: keep it out of diffs and reviews.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
